// S441 reproducer — addendum-3 T2: a component body reading its prop with `@` compiles clean when the component
// is `lift`ed from a `for`, then throws at load (the old tutorial 03-todos shape).
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch)
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/tut-component-prop-at-read-in-lift-throws.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: E-STATE-UNDECLARED, as the same component rendered DIRECTLY (`<TodoRow item=@one/>`) already gives:
//           "bare `@item` read with no reactive cell in scope". §15 props: "Props declared via `props` are in
//           scope throughout the entire component body" — read by bare name (§15 worked example `${name}`).
// Actual:   exit 0, no error. client.js: `_scrml_lift_tn_10.textContent = String((_scrml_cs_reactive_get("item").body) ?? "");`
//           EXECUTED (happy-dom, emitted html + runtime + client.js): `TypeError: undefined is not an object
//           (evaluating '_scrml_cs_reactive_get("item").body')`; the <ul> stays empty.
<program>
type Todo:struct = { id: number, body: string, done: boolean }
<items>: Todo[] = [{ id: 1, body: "a", done: true }]
const TodoRow = <li props={ item: Todo }>
    <input type="checkbox" checked=@item.done/>
    <span>${@item.body}</span>
</li>
<ul>
    ${
        for (let t of @items) {
            lift <TodoRow item=t/>
        }
    }
</ul>
</program>
